>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `filter_rewrites`

``` hol4
simpLib.filter_rewrites :
  ((simpLib.thname option * thm) -> bool) -> simpset -> simpset
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Removes the rewrites that a predicate rejects from a simpset.

`filter_rewrites keep ss` removes every rewrite `(name, th)`, as it was
added to `ss`, for which `keep` returns false. Everything else in `ss`
is kept, including the exclusions and settings that rebuilding from
`ssfrags_of ss` would lose.

### Failure

Never fails.

### Example

``` hol4
>> fun keep (_, th) = not (aconv (concl th) (concl AND_CLAUSES));
>>+ SIMP_CONV (simpLib.filter_rewrites keep bool_ss) [] “p ∧ T”;
>> SIMP_CONV (simpLib.filter_rewrites keep bool_ss) [] “p ∨ F”;
```

### See also

[`simpExtLib.clear_rules`](#simpExtLib.clear_rules),
[`simpLib.remove_ssfrags`](#simpLib.remove_ssfrags).
